    {
      "id": "14869000-0000-4000-8000-000000000053",
      "name": "Read first: research setup",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -40,
        -200
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 1,
        "width": 1100,
        "height": 580,
        "content": "### How it works\nManually discover up to ten Facebook groups from a topic and location brief using Apify. One bounded OpenAI batch assesses topic evidence from indexed names and snippets. The workflow canonicalizes URLs, retains query provenance, and upserts an evidence ledger in Google Sheets. Reviewer decisions and notes are never overwritten. A separate machine-generated Shortlist is replaced with at most five evidence-supported candidates. Empty discovery and malformed AI responses produce a readable execution result without sheet writes. An empty supported shortlist is valid.\n\nSearch qualifiers do not verify location, activity, privacy, permission or accessibility. Treat every candidate as research to review, never as permission to join, post or contact anyone. No Facebook credentials, member data or posts are used. Run manually only; this workflow stays inactive.\n\n### Setup\nAllow about ten minutes. Make a copy of the [sheet template](SHEET_TEMPLATE_PENDING_CREDENTIAL_REPAIR). Connect Apify, OpenAI and Google Sheets credentials. Put the copy's spreadsheet ID in node 1. Keep both tab names and headers unchanged. Customize the topic and brief there, then execute once manually. Install Apify node 0.9.0 on n8n 2.47.4 or newer. Each execution uses one Actor run capped at $0.05 and one gpt-5.4-mini batch (1200 output tokens maximum); verify current OpenAI pricing before running. No automatic retries or schedule are included."
      }
    }
